# A predicate's result is a bool, on every platform.
#
# startswith/endswith/has are the same kind of computation -- "answer yes or no" --
# so they must produce the same kind of value.  The Windows runtime built
# startswith/endswith with push_int while its own has/remove used push_bool, and the
# POSIX runtime used push_bool for all four, so str(startswith("abc","a")) answered
# "true" on Linux and "1" on Windows.  str() is the observable, so pin it here.
s = "  Hello World "
say("predbool "
    + str(startswith(s, "  "))
    + " " + str(endswith(s, " "))
    + " " + str(has("x", "y"))
    + " " + str(len(s)))
